      <body>
         <entry xml:id="epiqoros-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אפיקורוס</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾpyqwrws</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">epiqoros</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="epiqoros-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>heretic, sceptic, unbeliever</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>Ἐπίκουρος</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>[והנחש היה ערום מכל חית וגו'] ר' הושעיא רבה אמר דיקרטיס היה עומד כקנה ורגלים יש לו, ר' ירמיה בן אלעזר אמר אפיקורוס [היה], ר' שמעון בן אלעזר אמר כגמל היה, טובה גדולה חסר העולם שאילולי כן היה אדם משלח פרגמטיא בידו והיה הולך ובא.</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">19,1</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 171: 2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פרגמטיא</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">דיקרטיס</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Hoshaʿaya the Elder said: He stood out distinguished [erect] like a reed, and he had feet. R. Yirmeyah b. Elʿazar said: He was an unbeliever. R. Shimʿon ben Elʿazar said: He was like a camel. He deprived the world of much good, for had this not happened, one could have sent his merchandise through him, and he would have gone and returned. (Freedman / Simon 149)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 25 [8c: 46]</bibl>; <bibl type="ancient">BerRbti 2,3 [41: 13]</bibl></note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>See <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 104ab</bibl>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>107b-108a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
